  "_about": "a budgerigar: a small slim parakeet, half its length a long graduated blue tail -- the wild bird grass-green beneath, the yellow face and forehead with a row of black spots across the throat and a violet patch on each cheek, the crown, nape, back and wings barred black on yellow (scalloped on the wing); the small hooked horn-coloured bill under the blue cere of a cock; grey feet, two toes forward and two back. Coats: green, blue, lutino, the hen's brown cere. (rework/passerines/passerines.py) (2026-11-08, review.py: bill) The bill: the parrot's two mandibles scaled onto this one's roots -- the upper's hook bent down to end a little below and before the lower's tip (it curled back into a C round a hole), the lower a deep scoop fitting into its curve (it was a block).",
